.TH WHITELIST-BYPASS 1 "September 2026" "whitelist-bypass" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
whitelist-bypass \- Multi-account orchestrator for WhitelistBypass headless creators
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whitelist-bypass
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIUSER\fR] [\fB\-\-qr\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whitelist-bypass
is a multi-tenant orchestrator and lifecycle manager for the WhitelistBypass project.
It encapsulates L4 network traffic (TCP/UDP) over WebRTC sessions (such as Yandex.Telemost,
VK Calls, WB Stream, or DION) to circumvent network whitelisting and censorship.
.PP
Each user operates under a strict 1:1:1 model (1 User = 1 Service Account / Cookies = 1 Conference Room = 1 Isolated Creator Instance).
Links are semi-persistent and maintained across regular service restarts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBlink\fR, \fBget-link\fR \fIUSER\fR [\fB\-\-qr\fR]
Display the current conference URI, tunnel provider, and service status for the specified user. If \fB\-\-qr\fR is given, also displays the conference URI as an ANSI UTF-8 QR code directly in the terminal.
.TP
\fBqr\fR \fIUSER\fR
Generate and display an ANSI UTF-8 QR code in the terminal for the user's active conference room, followed by the textual URL.
.TP
\fBrotate\fR \fIUSER\fR [\fB\-\-qr\fR]
Request a new clean conference room from the platform SFU. Stops the current instance, clears previous room tokens, launches a fresh daemon, captures the newly generated link using native \fB\-\-write\-file\fR, and saves it into \fBroom.env\fR. If \fB\-\-qr\fR is given, also displays the newly created link as a QR code.
.TP
\fBprovider\fR, \fBset\-provider\fR \fIUSER\fR \fIPROVIDER\fR [\fB\-\-rotate\fR]
Change the active WebRTC platform provider (\fBtelemost\fR, \fBvk\fR, \fBwbstream\fR, \fBdion\fR) in the user's \fBuser.conf\fR. If \fB\-\-rotate\fR is specified, immediately stops the current session, launches the new provider daemon, creates a fresh conference room, and displays its QR code.
.TP
\fBlist\fR
Print a summary table of all configured users, their configured providers, current systemd service statuses, and active room links.
.TP
\fBstart\fR \fIUSER\fR
Start the systemd unit \fBwhitelist-bypass@\fIUSER\fR.service.
.TP
\fBstop\fR \fIUSER\fR
Stop the systemd unit \fBwhitelist-bypass@\fIUSER\fR.service.
.TP
\fBrestart\fR \fIUSER\fR
Restart the systemd unit \fBwhitelist-bypass@\fIUSER\fR.service.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR \fIUSER\fR
Display detailed systemd service status for \fBwhitelist-bypass@\fIUSER\fR.service.
.TP
\fBis-active\fR \fIUSER\fR
Check whether the service is currently active (\fBactive\fR or \fBinactive\fR).
.TP
\fBrun\fR \fIUSER\fR
Internal entrypoint executed by the systemd service template. Resolves user configuration, determines the target creator binary, assembles arguments, and replaces the shell process with the creator daemon.
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Display command usage summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output all command results in structured, machine-readable JSON format.
.TP
\fB\-\-qr\fR, \fB\-q\fR
Render an ANSI UTF-8 QR code directly in the terminal for room links.
.TP
\fB\-\-rotate\fR, \fB\-r\fR
When changing providers via \fBprovider\fR, immediately rotate and provision a new room.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Each user is configured in their own subdirectory under \fI/etc/whitelist-bypass/users/<username>/\fR:
.TP
\fBuser.conf\fR
User-specific parameters in key=value format:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPROVIDER\fR: Target platform (\fBtelemost\fR, \fBvk\fR, \fBwbstream\fR, \fBdion\fR). Default is \fBtelemost\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRESOURCES\fR: Memory and GC profile (\fBdefault\fR, \fBmoderate\fR, \fBunlimited\fR). Default is \fBdefault\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUPSTREAM_SOCKS\fR: Optional upstream SOCKS5 proxy (e.g. \fB127.0.0.1:1080\fR) for routing unblocked egress traffic.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTELEGRAM_ID\fR: Optional numeric Telegram user ID for automated bot identity resolution.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBVK_ID\fR: Optional numeric VK user ID for automated bot identity resolution.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDEBUG\fR: Enable verbose diagnostic logging (\fBtrue\fR or \fBfalse\fR).
.RE
.TP
\fBcookies-$provider.json\fR, \fBcookies.json\fR
Session cookies exported from the browser for the user's account (must be >15 bytes).
.TP
\fBroom.env\fR
Environment file containing the active \fBCALL_LINK\fR. Managed automatically by the \fBrotate\fR command.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/usr/local/bin/whitelist-bypass\fR
The main orchestrator executable.
.TP
\fI/run/whitelist-bypass/core.sock\fR
Unix Domain Socket for local REST API and Core daemon communication.
.TP
\fI/etc/systemd/system/whitelist-bypass-core.service\fR
Core daemon systemd service unit.
.TP
\fI/etc/systemd/system/whitelist-bypass@.service\fR
Template systemd service unit for user tunnels.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Create or rotate room for user 'danya':
.RS
# whitelist-bypass rotate danya
.RE
.PP
.B Check all configured users:
.RS
# whitelist-bypass list
.RE
.PP
.B Retrieve current link:
.RS
# whitelist-bypass get-link danya
.RE
.PP
.B Display terminal QR code:
.RS
# whitelist-bypass qr danya
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
